            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_647325af">B2:413</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="da">Da den højstsalige Konge, Frederik den Femte skulde føres til sit Hvilested, blev paa det kongelige Universitet følgende Klage-Sange opførte</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_70437d49">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_20">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="_22">Johannes Ewald</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="_21">King Frederik V</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_23_0">
               <date isodate="1766" xml:id="date_f3884338">1766</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_23_0">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_23_0">
               <p xml:id="idm124">When <persName xml:id="idm125" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Frederik V</persName> died in January 1766, Scheibe was asked to compose the music for the official church service; however, he was also asked by the University of Copenhagen to compose another mourning cantata to another text by the young poet <persName xml:id="idm126" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johannes Ewald</persName>. The chancellor, <persName xml:id="idm127" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Christian Gottlieb Kratzenstein</persName>, had asked Ewald to write a text to which he agreed, and Scheibe offered to compose the music for 30 Rigsdaler. However, a few days earlier the cantor at the Latin school, <persName xml:id="idm128" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Nissen</persName>, had handed in his own text for a cantata, which was sent to <persName xml:id="idm129" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Andreas Cramer</persName>, the royal Chaplain who thought it to be of a rather poor quality. The Senate discussed whether it would be possible to ask Scheibe to supply the music without offending Nissen who would be a singer in the cantata as well as leading the performance. Scheibe would only be present at the rehearsals though some members thought it would better also to let Scheibe lead the performance. On the morning of 18 March, the cantata was performed by the university’s collegium musicum consisting of both strings and woodwinds and a large choir, that is on the same day as the official church service took place.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_8f039859">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="listBibl_a84c74c4-a2c5-4d41-993c-b84040743152266">
               <head xml:id="head_92191c70">Bibliography</head>
               <bibl label="" xml:id="bibl_da712c72">
                  <genre xml:id="genre_6143652e">article</genre>
                  <genre xml:id="genre_6dace125">newspaper</genre>
                  <annot xml:id="annot_6b0bcb94">
                     <p xml:id="idm138">
                        <lb xml:id="idm139"/>'Den 18 Martii blev paa den øverste Høre-Sahl ved den Kongl. Kiøbenhavnske Høye Skole, holdet en ziirlig Tale af Hans Magnificence h. a. Rector Academiæ, Hr. Professor Kratzenstein, i Overværelse af Hans Excellence Hr. Geheime-Raad Thott, som Academiets høye Patron, tillige med den hele Academiske Øvrighed og et stort Antall Tilhørere. For og efter Talen, som holdtes om Formiddagen, blev af endeel Studentere opført en smuk Sørge-Musiqve, som bestod af alle Slags strygende, blæsende og klingende Instrumenter, og et tallrige Synge-Chor. Digten var sammensat af Msr. Ewald, og ved Musiqven udtrykt af Hr. Capellmester Scheibe.'</p>
                  </annot>
                  <title level="a" xml:id="title_faf23181"/>
                  <title level="j" xml:id="title_3a585284">Kiøbenhavns Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger</title>
                  <imprint xml:id="imprint_4d3aafb5">
                     <date isodate="1766-03-20" xml:id="date_ce927050">1766-03-20</date>
                  </imprint>
               </bibl>
               <bibl label="" xml:id="bibl_96a8bbba">
                  <genre xml:id="genre_9b1b2d60">article</genre>
                  <genre xml:id="genre_c1733350">newspaper</genre>
                  <annot xml:id="annot_9a91a1cc">
                     <p xml:id="idm148">
                        <lb xml:id="idm149"/>Regarding publications: '[...] udkommen fra Hans Kongelige Majestæts og Universitets Bogtrykkerie sælges der for 4 ß. - Klage-Sange opførte af Cantor Nissen paa det Kongelige Universitet den 18 Martii, hvortil Poesien er af Mr. Johannes Ewald og Musiqven af Hr. Capelmester Scheibe.'</p>
                  </annot>
